## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant data ingestion architecture across AWS accounts while addressing security, reliability, and cost optimization challenges.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles with trust relationships
- Tenant isolation through data partitioning and access controls
- Exactly-once processing using idempotent operations
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Firehose, and S3 integration
- KMS encryption and data retention policies
- Cost management through throttling and lifecycle strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Idempotent processor using DynamoDB for deduplication
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const dynamodb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const failures = [];

  for (const record of event.Records) {
    const { tenantId, sequenceId, data } = JSON.parse(record.kinesis.data);
    const tableName = process.env.DDB_TABLE;

    try {
      // Check if sequence already processed
      const result = await dynamodb.get({
        TableName: tableName,
        Key: { tenantId, sequenceId }
      }).promise();

      if (result.Item) {
        continue; // Skip duplicate
      }

      // Process data...
      await processData(tenantId, data);

      // Mark as processed
      await dynamodb.put({
        TableName: tableName,
        Item: { tenantId, sequenceId, processedAt: Date.now() }
      }).promise();

    } catch (error) {
      failures.push({ itemIdentifier: record.kinesis.sequenceNumber });
    }
  }

  return { batchItemFailures: failures };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design secure cross-account workflows using ABAC, STS, KMS, and tenant isolation. It emphasizes least privilege, tenant isolation, and compliance requirements—critical skills for building enterprise-grade data pipelines.

## Key Concepts

- **IAM tag-based access control (ABAC)** – Use tags to grant access based on attributes
- **STS AssumeRole with session tags** – Pass tenant-id via aws:PrincipalTag and aws:SessionTag for attribute-based authorization
- **KMS key policy** – Condition access on matching session/principal tags
- **S3 bucket policy** – Enforce TLS-only, SSE-KMS, and no public access
- **Cognito JWT validation** – Authenticate device requests

## Trust Policy (Processing Lambda Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:SourceAccount": "123456789012"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Permission Policy (Processing Lambda Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::*:role/TenantRole*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        },
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Trust Policy (Compliance Tenant Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/ProcessingLambdaRole"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "sts:ExternalId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}",
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Permission Policy (Compliance Tenant Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "aws:kms",
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## KMS Key Policy

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::*:role/TenantRole*"
      },
      "Action": "kms:Encrypt",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "kms:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## S3 Bucket Policy

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:PublicAccess": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Test Plan

| Test Case | Description | Expected Result |
|-----------|-------------|------------------|
| **1. Valid JWT with tenant-a** | Send request with valid Cognito JWT for tenant-a | Lambda assumes TenantRole-a, writes to tenant-a/ partition |
| **2. Invalid JWT** | Send request with expired/invalid JWT | API Gateway rejects with 401 Unauthorized |
| **3. Cross-tenant access attempt** | Lambda for tenant-a attempts to write to tenant-b path | Access denied - principal tag mismatch |
| **4. Non-TLS connection** | Attempt PUT over HTTP | S3 bucket policy denies request |
| **5. KMS key access by untagged role** | Role without tenant-id tag attempts encryption | KMS policy denies encryption |
| **6. Public access attempt** | Attempt to access bucket publicly | Bucket policy denies - no public access enforced |
| **7. Session tag verification** | Verify STS passes tenant-id as session tag | CloudTrail shows aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id matches aws:SessionTag/tenant-id |
| **8. Parquet file verification** | Write and read back Parquet files | Files correctly partitioned by date and tenant |

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design scalable multi-tenant data isolation using AWS IAM, Lake Formation, and S3 policies across multiple regions. It explores understanding of cross-region replication, governance controls, and auditability for SaaS applications.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped IAM roles with STS AssumeRole session tags
- Lake Formation permissions and data lake zone isolation
- S3 replication, encryption (SSE-KMS), and access boundaries
- Least-privilege access enforcement through bucket policies
- Auditing with CloudTrail, AWS Config, and Access Analyzer

## Code Example
```javascript
// Trust policy snippet for tenant role
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::${tenant_account_id}:role/TenantUser"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${tenant_id}"},
      "StringLike": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${tenant_id}"}
    }
  }]
}

// S3 bucket policy for tenant isolation
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Deny",
    "Principal": "*",
    "Action": "s3:*",
    "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::datalake-bucket/*",
    "Condition": {
      "StringNotEquals": {"s3:prefix": ["${tenant_id}/*"]},
      "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}
    }
  }]
}
```
